From aec9a453a883665fe838c80d09b89d226631139a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: z060142 <z060142@yahoo.com.tw>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 04:11:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 203/225] feat: glossy (rough) triangle-RT reflections -
 shaders (decision 08)

One GGX visible-normal sample per ray traced pixel per frame, plus the temporal
and spatial reconstruction that makes one sample usable.

CommonSVO_RT.cfi
  - SVO_RTParams2 (glossyMode, glossScale, temporalFrames, blueNoiseBound) and the
    VOX_RT_MIRROR_GLOSS / VOX_RT_GLOSS_BAND constants every RT pass keys on.
  - SVO_BlueNoise at t32 (64x64 RGBA8, read with Load, no sampler) plus an integer
    hash fallback, and RT_BlueNoise4: two uniform pairs per pixel, decorrelated in
    time by a per-frame R4 golden-ratio offset on SVO_FrameIdByte.
  - RT_SmoothnessToAlpha: CE's OWN mapping, alpha = (1 - smoothness)^2, taken from
    shadeLib.cfi SmoothnessToRoughness + SpecularBRDF, so the traced lobe is the
    lobe the deferred pass shades the same surface with.
  - RT_SampleGGXVNDF (Heitz 2018 listing 1), RT_SmithLambda, RT_GGXWeightG2overG1
    and RT_GlossyReflectDir: sample, reflect, resample once if the sample went
    below the surface, else fall back to the mirror direction.

Total_Illumination.cfx
  - ConeTracePS: below smoothness 0.98 the ray is the GGX sample instead of the
    mirror direction. The VNDF estimator weight G2/G1 leaves the pass in the
    LENGTH of RayDir.xyz - a free lane, the direction being unit by construction.
    Fresnel is deliberately NOT in the weight: TiledShading.cfi:951-953 applies
    the reflecting surface's envFresnel downstream, so F0 is applied exactly once.
  - ShadePS: recovers the weight and the unit direction, multiplies the whole
    reflected radiance (hit shading and miss sky alike) by it.
  - DemosaicPS: temporal accumulation for RT pixels - reprojection through the
    VIRTUAL REFLECTED POSITION (the pixel reprojected at surface depth + hit
    distance, lerped back to surface depth as the lobe widens), roughness
    dependent history length (2 frames at mirror, e_svoTI_RT_TemporalFrames at the
    rough end), GetBlendMin's depth-ratio and off-screen rejection, a 3x3
    neighbourhood variance clamp on the history, and a hard reset off screen.
  - UpScalePS: the single tap becomes a roughness-scaled bilateral, radius 0 at
    mirror to 4 source texels at the bottom of the RT range, with a new
    hit-distance similarity weight on top of the existing depth and normal tests.
  - RT_IsTriPixel's gloss gate drops by the cross-fade band half width, and
    UpScalePS ramps the RT result off the diffuse GI anchor across the band, so
    the switch from voxel cone tracing to triangle rays has no hard seam.
  - Debug 14 = the raw 1 spp trace with both filters off, 15 = the temporal
    history weight.

Every hunk is inside %_RT_QUALITY / bRTPixel or folds away off the flag; no
file-scope %-flag #if. cryfx_lint.py clean, rtharness2 17/17 compiles.

